#
# \brief  Sponge DE QGenodeScreen 1x1-stale race probe (Phase 14 W3 / D14.8(b))
# \author Sponge OS contributors
# \date   2026
#
# Focused cold-boot reproducer for the QGenodeScreen 1x1-stale race
# that the Phase 11 alpha-flake review suspected
# (docs/evidence/task-6-phase11-alpha-flake.md). The Phase 11 fix
# added a width-floor guard in panel_widget.cc::_apply_geometry
# (width = screen_w > 64 ? screen_w : 1024); this scenario is the
# instrument D14.8(b) requires to decide whether a follow-up vendored
# patch to QGenodeScreen is in-scope or Re-scoped.
#
# Topology (modeled on the proven base-sel4 interactive reference
# run/sponge-de-sel4-interactive.run, MINUS the launch/inject plumbing
# — no sponge_pkgd, no pkg_runtime, no input-relay ROM, no QMP
# choreography):
#
#   init
#   + timer
#   + nitpicker         (Gui/Capture/Event)
#   + drivers           (sub-init; vesa_fb + ps2 + usb_hid + xHCI +
#                        event_filter + acpi + pci_decode + platform;
#                        carries the same interactive-PC stack as
#                        run/sponge-de-sel4-interactive.run so cold-
#                        boot timing matches the proven reference)
#   + sponge-de         (caps: 1000 / ram: 128M; same proven sizing
#                        from run/sponge-de-sel4-interactive.run —
#                        the Phase 10 §11.1 capability-exhaustion
#                        fix that closed the original EGL-on-seL4
#                        hang)
#   + qscreen_race_probe (a small plain-Genode component;
#                        repos/sponge/src/test/qscreen_race_probe/;
#                        reads nitpicker's composited pixels through
#                        a Capture session, polls a 60s cold-boot
#                        window for the demo-domain themed window_bg
#                        color, then logs
#                          qscreen-race-probe: trial verdict clean|race
#                        — the run script gates on that regex)
#
# What this scenario proves / does not prove:
#
#   PROVES — the FIRST capture sample after component construction
#   (no warm-up) on a heavy seL4 topology:
#     (a) the panel band (512,14) reads 0x0 (black, 1x28-degenerate
#         race signature) OR 0x1e1e2e (nitpicker bg, normal pre-paint
#         state), AND
#     (b) within a bounded 60s cold-boot window, the demo-domain
#         center (512,412) either paints the themed window_bg
#         #313244 (race did NOT reproduce) OR stays at nitpicker bg
#         forever (race DID reproduce — the panel-construction 1x1
#         path pinned Qt to a screen it cannot recover from without
#         a follow-up geometry event).
#   DOES NOT — apply any vendored-tree patch (AGENTS.md §5.2 — W3
#   is an investigation workstream, not a fix workstream; per the
#   plan). The verdict lines from the 10 trials are the input D14.8(b)
#   uses to decide.
#
# Automated verification: a single regex gate on the probe's verdict
# line (the run tool records the trial as PASS for both "clean" and
# "race" verdicts; the verdict content is consumed by the evidence
# log, not by a hard pass/fail gate — per D14.8(b) "≥ 3 of 10 cold-
# boot trials" is a counting policy, not a hard threshold).
#
# Kernel matrix: base-sel4 only (the race is an seL4 timing-class
# symptom; base-linux's Genode core runs init synchronously and
# nitpicker's panorama info is always ready before sponge-de
# constructs).
#

assert {[have_spec sel4]} \
	"sponge-de-qscreen-race-probe requires KERNEL=sel4 (BOARD=pc) in build.conf. \
	 The QGenodeScreen 1x1-stale race is an seL4 timing-class symptom; \
	 base-linux's core runs init synchronously and never reproduces."

build { core lib/ld init timer server/report_rom server/nitpicker \
         driver/acpi app/pci_decode driver/platform \
         driver/framebuffer/vesa driver/ps2 \
         driver/usb_host/pc driver/usb_hid \
         server/event_filter \
         sponge-de test/qscreen_race_probe \
         qt6/base lib/libc lib/libm lib/stdcxx lib/mesa \
         lib/mesa_gpu-softpipe lib/egl lib/softpipe lib/libdrm lib/expat \
         lib/qt6_component lib/vfs lib/vfs_pipe lib/vfs_gpu lib/rom_filter \
         lib/zlib lib/libpng lib/blit }

create_boot_directory

install_config {
config
+ parent-provides
  + service ROM
  + service PD
  + service RM
  + service CPU
  + service LOG
  + service IRQ
  + service IO_MEM
  + service IO_PORT

+ default | caps: 200 | ram: 4M
+ default-route
  + any-service
    + parent
    + any-child

+ start timer
  + provides | + service Timer

+ start report_rom | caps: 100 | ram: 4M
  + provides
    + service Report
    + service ROM
  + config | verbose: no

+ start nitpicker | ram: 16M
  + provides
    + service Gui
    + service Capture
    + service Event
  + route
    + service Report | + child report_rom
    + service Timer  | + child timer
    + any-service
      + parent
      + any-child
  + config
    + capture
    + event
    + domain panel | layer: 1 | content: client | label: no
                   | hover: always | focus: click | ypos: 0 | height: 28
    + domain launcher | layer: 4 | content: client | label: no
                      | hover: always | focus: click
                      | xpos: 0 | ypos: 28 | width: 341 | height: 480
    + domain demo | layer: 2 | content: client | label: no
                  | hover: always | focus: click
                  | xpos: 192 | ypos: 172 | width: 640 | height: 480
    + domain default | layer: 3 | content: client | label: no
                     | hover: always | focus: click | ypos: 28 | height: -28
    + policy | label_prefix: sponge-de -> Sponge Panel   | domain: panel
    + policy | label_prefix: sponge-de -> Sponge Launcher | domain: launcher
    + policy | label_prefix: sponge-de -> Sponge DE Demo | domain: demo
    + default-policy | domain: default
    + background | color: #1e1e2e

+ start drivers | caps: 1500 | ram: 96M | managing_system: yes
  + binary init
  + route
    + service ROM | label: config | + parent | label: drivers.config
    + service Timer               | + child timer
    + service Capture             | + child nitpicker
    + service Event               | + child nitpicker
    + any-service                 | + parent
  + config
    + parent-provides
      + service IRQ
      + service IO_MEM
      + service IO_PORT
      + service ROM
      + service PD
      + service RM
      + service CPU
      + service LOG
      + service Timer
      + service Capture
      + service Event

    + default | caps: 60

    + start acpi | caps: 250 | ram: 4M
      + route
        + service IO_MEM | + parent
        + service LOG    | + parent
        + service PD     | + parent
        + service RM     | + parent
        + service CPU    | + parent
        + service ROM    | + parent
        + service Report | + child report_rom

    + start report_rom | caps: 100 | ram: 2M
      + provides
      | + service ROM
      | + service Report
      + config
      | + policy | label: pci_decode -> system | report: acpi -> acpi
      | + policy | label: platform -> devices  | report: pci_decode -> devices
      | + policy | label: usb_hid -> report    | report: usb -> devices
      + route
        + service LOG | + parent
        + service PD  | + parent
        + service CPU | + parent
        + service ROM | + parent

    + start pci_decode | caps: 100 | ram: 2M
      + route
        + service Report              | + child report_rom
        + service ROM | label: system | + child report_rom
        + service IO_MEM              | + parent
        + service LOG                 | + parent
        + service PD                  | + parent
        + service RM                  | + parent
        + service CPU                 | + parent
        + service ROM                 | + parent

    + start platform | caps: 200 | ram: 3M | managing_system: yes
      + provides
      | + service Dma
      | + service Platform
      + route
      | + service ROM | label: devices | + child report_rom
      | + service Report               | + child report_rom
      | + service IRQ                  | + parent
      | + service IO_MEM               | + parent
      | + service IO_PORT              | + parent
      | + service ROM                  | + parent
      | + service PD                   | + parent
      | + service CPU                  | + parent
      | + service LOG                  | + parent
      | + service Timer                | + parent
      + config
        + report | devices: yes
        + policy | label_prefix: ps2             | + device ps2
        + policy | label_prefix: fb  | info: yes | + pci | class: VGA
        + policy | label_prefix: usb | info: yes | + pci | class: USB

    + start fb | caps: 150 | ram: 20M
      + binary vesa_fb
      + route
        + service ROM | label: config | + parent | label: fb.config
        + service Report              | + child report_rom
        + service Dma                 | + child platform
        + service Platform            | + child platform
        + service IO_PORT             | + parent
        + service IO_MEM              | + parent
        + service ROM                 | + parent
        + service PD                  | + parent
        + service CPU                 | + parent
        + service LOG                 | + parent
        + service Timer               | + parent
        + service Capture             | + parent

    + start ps2 | caps: 100 | ram: 1280K
      + config
      + route
        + service Dma      | + child platform
        + service Platform | + child platform
        + service Event    | + child event_filter | label: ps2
        + service ROM      | + parent
        + service PD       | + parent
        + service CPU      | + parent
        + service LOG      | + parent
        + service Timer    | + parent

    + start usb | caps: 200 | ram: 16M
      + binary pc_usb_host
      + provides | + service Usb
      + config
      | + report | devices: yes
      | + policy | label_prefix: usb_hid | + device | class: 0x3
      + route
        + service Dma                     | + child platform
        + service Platform                | + child platform
        + service Report | label: devices | + child report_rom
        + service ROM                     | + parent
        + service PD                      | + parent
        + service RM                      | + parent
        + service CPU                     | + parent
        + service LOG                     | + parent
        + service Timer                   | + parent

    + start usb_hid | caps: 180 | ram: 10M
      + route
        + service ROM | label: report | + child report_rom
        + service ROM                 | + parent
        + service PD                  | + parent
        + service RM                  | + parent
        + service CPU                 | + parent
        + service LOG                 | + parent
        + service Timer               | + parent
        + service Event               | + child event_filter | label: usb
        + service Usb                 | + child usb

    + start event_filter | caps: 90 | ram: 1280K
      + provides | + service Event
      + route
        + service ROM | label: config | + parent | label: event_filter.config
        + service Event               | + parent
        + service ROM                 | + parent
        + service PD                  | + parent
        + service CPU                 | + parent
        + service LOG                 | + parent
        + service Timer               | + parent

+ start sponge-de | caps: 1000 | ram: 128M
  + config
    + vfs
      + dir dev
        + log
        + inline rtc | : 2018-01-01 00:01
      + dir pipe | + pipe
      + tar qt6_dejavusans.tar
      + tar qt6_libqgenode.tar
    + libc | stdout: /dev/log | stderr: /dev/log | pipe: /pipe | rtc: /dev/rtc
  + route
    + service Gui | label_last: Sponge Panel   | + child nitpicker
    + service Gui | label_last: Sponge Launcher | + child nitpicker
    + service Gui                              | + child nitpicker
    + service Report | label: shape  | + child report_rom
    + service ROM | label: default.theme        | + parent
    + service ROM | label: mesa_gpu.lib.so | + parent | label: mesa_gpu-softpipe.lib.so
    + any-service
      + parent
      + any-child

+ start qscreen_race_probe | caps: 100 | ram: 16M
  + route
    + service Capture | + child nitpicker
    + service Timer   | + child timer
    + any-service
      + parent
      + any-child
- }

#
# Stage every non-build-artifact boot module into bin/ BEFORE
# build_boot_image (base-sel4 packs image.elf in one shot; modules
# added after build_boot_image never reach the guest — Phase 10 §11.2
# item 3 / docs/11-environment.md §10.4).
#
exec mkdir -p bin

#
# qt6_dejavusans.tar is not a build output; source-build it from the
# qt6_base port's bundled DejaVuSans.ttf (mirrors
# repos/libports/recipes/raw/qt6_dejavusans/).
#
set dejavu_dst "bin/qt6_dejavusans.tar"
if {![file exists $dejavu_dst]} {
	set dejavu_src [glob -nocomplain "${genode_dir}/contrib/qt6_base-*/src/lib/qt6_base/src/3rdparty/wasm/DejaVuSans.ttf"]
	if {[llength $dejavu_src] == 0} {
		error "DejaVuSans.ttf not found in the qt6_base port sources"
	}
	set staging "[run_dir]/dejavusans-staging"
	file mkdir "$staging/qt/lib/fonts"
	file copy -force [lindex $dejavu_src 0] "$staging/qt/lib/fonts/DejaVuSans.ttf"
	exec tar -cf $dejavu_dst -C $staging qt
	file delete -force $staging
}

#
# Driver sub-init config modules (vendored recipes/raw/drivers_interactive-pc/).
#
set recipe_dir "${genode_dir}/repos/os/recipes/raw/drivers_interactive-pc"
foreach f { drivers.config fb.config } {
	if {![file exists "$recipe_dir/$f"]} {
		error "$recipe_dir/$f missing (vendored drivers_interactive-pc recipe drifted?)"
	}
	exec cp -f "$recipe_dir/$f" "bin/$f"
}

#
# event_filter.config — copy the vendored recipe verbatim (this
# scenario does not exercise input so the W3 accelerate-removal
# deviation is unnecessary; the standard recipe is fine and matches
# every other Phase 10+ base-sel4 interactive scenario for symmetry).
#
exec cp -f "${genode_dir}/repos/os/recipes/raw/drivers_interactive-pc/event_filter.config" \
           "bin/event_filter.config"

#
# Chargen ROM modules (event_filter keyboard map).
#
set chargen_dir "${genode_dir}/repos/os/src/server/event_filter"
foreach f { en_us.chargen special.chargen } {
	if {![file exists "$chargen_dir/$f"]} {
		error "$chargen_dir/$f missing (event_filter sources drifted?)"
	}
	exec cp -f "$chargen_dir/$f" "bin/$f"
}

#
# Default theme ROM module.
#
exec cp -f "${genode_dir}/repos/sponge/src/sponge-de/themes/default.theme" \
           "bin/default.theme"

#
# Full boot module list (every non-build-artifact module staged
# explicitly; matches run/sponge-de-sel4-interactive.run's pattern).
#
set boot_modules [build_artifacts]
foreach m { libQt6Core.lib.so libQt6Gui.lib.so libQt6Widgets.lib.so \
            libqgenode.lib.so qt6_libqgenode.tar qt6_dejavusans.tar \
            drivers.config fb.config event_filter.config \
            en_us.chargen special.chargen \
            default.theme } {
	lappend boot_modules $m
}

build_boot_image $boot_modules

#
# QEMU: base-sel4 needs >= 1 GiB guest RAM (seL4 SKIM window + kernel
# structures; docs/11-environment.md §7.2). The drivers sub-init +
# sponge-de sizing stays at the proven reference budget. -nographic
# keeps it headless (serial only). NO -qmp: the probe does not
# require host-driven input — the only variable under test is the
# cold-boot timing race, and adding QMP machinery would introduce
# its own timing noise (TCP connect latency, expect round-trips).
#
append qemu_args " -nographic -m 2G "

#
# Automated verification (D14.8(b) instrument):
#
#   (1) DISPLAY: vesa_fb sets the mode and maps the physical VESA
#       framebuffer (vesa_fb is consuming nitpicker's Capture session,
#       i.e. driving the real display with nitpicker's composited
#       output). The Phase 10 §11.1 capability-exhaustion fix that
#       closed the original EGL-on-seL4 hang uses the same 1024x768
#       mode-set gate.
#   (2) QSCREEN VERDICT: the probe logs
#         qscreen-race-probe: trial verdict clean|race
#       exactly once per trial. The regex below matches BOTH
#       verdicts — the evidence log applies D14.8(b)'s counting
#       policy ("race" if >= 3 of 10 trials reproduce the 1x1-stale
#       symptom, otherwise "Re-scoped"). A trial that never reaches
#       a verdict line within the bounded window fails loud (the
#       run_genode_until timeout means the probe hung, which is
#       itself a race signature worth recording in the evidence log
#       as a separate "hang" verdict).
#
# Note: this scenario intentionally does NOT mirror the proven
# reference's second gate (`Connected device.*POINTER.*` from usb_hid).
# The race probe does not exercise input — adding the xHCI + usb-tablet
# QEMU devices would introduce boot-timing noise that swamps the
# single-frame race signal the probe is trying to measure. Dropping
# usb_hid also lets the scenario run faster (the proven reference's
# 600s+ budget includes input-driver bring-up).
#
run_genode_until {.*\[init -> drivers -> fb\] using 1024x768.*} 90
run_genode_until {.*qscreen-race-probe: trial verdict (clean|race).*} 90